<div class="page">
  <% --[[ A header rather than a section: the vertical rhythm rule would add a margin above the first
          thing on the page, and this block already carries its own. ]] %>
  <header class="wtitle">
    <h1>Dev Workspace</h1>
    <p>The WarcraftXL toolchain in one window. Every tool works on the same client, reports through
      the same jobs and undoes itself the same way, so building for WarcraftXL is the work rather
      than the setting up around it.</p>
  </header>

  <section><%- status %></section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec"><h2>Your tools</h2><span class="spacer"></span>
      <span class="aside">the rail on the left has everything</span></div>

    <% --[[ Kept, not catalogued. Which tools exist is the rail's job and the picker's; this grid is
            the handful you run, in the order you added them. ]] %>
    <%- favourites %>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec"><h2>Activity</h2></div>
    <div class="panel">
      <% --[[ The slot the runner fills. Empty is the honest state until a tool that writes exists,
              and it is worth showing rather than hiding because it is where a restore will be. ]] %>
      <div class="empty bare">
        <b>Nothing has run yet</b>
        <span>Jobs started here stay on this list when you navigate away, with what they moved and
          the way back.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
